Done. This iteration completed **T026** — the test-first task for User Story 2's failure matrix.

**What I did:** Created `lib/test_prime_pipeline.py`, a new end-to-end test suite that drives `proposer.sh` with a fake Prime launcher through all nine failure classes (launch failure, nonzero exit, signal, timeout, provider auth/model error with exit 0, empty stream, malformed/truncated stream, parser failure). It asserts each pass produces exactly one durable `result.json` with the correct `reason_code`/`status` and one equivalent `agent_result` event, plus breaker behavior (halts at exactly N launches, never N+1) and one-terminal-per-pass.

**Why they fail (correctly):** All 13 tests fail for substantive contract gaps, not harness errors — the pipeline currently pipes the producer into the tap and unconditionally `return 0`s, and the tap suppresses `agent_result` when an invocation context is present, so no `result.json` and no terminal event exist for Prime invocations yet. These are exactly the gaps that T030–T035 will close.

I followed the test conventions from `test_prime_backend.py` (fake launcher via `$WIGGUM_PRIME_AGENT_BIN`, sanitized fixtures, no real credentials or `/root/` paths, absolute evidence paths) and targeted the reason-code vocabulary already defined in `lib/invocation_result.py`. Checkbox T026 is flipped to `- [x]`.
