T082 is complete. Here's what happened.

## T082 — two real dual-role Prime validations: done

I executed both required real runs on this host (all infra live: Prime binaries, Loki :3100, OTLP collector :4318), and both reached `# DONE — all 1 phase(s) approved` with nonce-bound `APPROVED` critic verdicts and tools disabled on the critic:

- **Stock** (`--proposer prime --critic prime`), run id `20260810-171657-3393894`
- **Fleet** (`--proposer prime:compass --critic prime:compass`), run id `20260810-171730-3395240`

The stock prime-agent's *default* provider (OpenAI) is uncredentialed on this host and fails closed with a precise `provider_auth` reason — the instrumentation worked, the key didn't. I used the documented `WIGGUM_PRIME_AGENT_BIN` escape hatch to point stock prime-agent at the credentialed gateway (provider/model only, nothing else changed), which is the honest way to exercise the identical stock code path against a working provider.

**Query-verified across all three sinks by run id**: local JSONL had 100% of events; `{job="ralph"} | logfmt | run_id=…` on Loki retrieved every agent-stream event plus lifecycle events; the OTLP-forwarded copy (`service_name="ralph"`) returned exactly 2× the direct-push count, proving OTLP independently carried the same correlation. No `thinking`/canary content leaked. Evidence recorded in `quickstart.md` §"Recorded Dual-Role Real-Run Evidence (T082)".

### One real bug found and fixed along the way

Verifying the queries surfaced a genuine, contract-violating gap that would have made T082's own acceptance impossible to honestly claim: `LocalFirstFanout` shipped the **pre-envelope** fields to Loki/OTLP, so agent-stream events reached the remote sinks **without `run_id`** — a run_id-scoped query retrieved only the 7 orchestrator lifecycle events, not the agent activity. The parity test passed only because its sample event carried `run_id` inline and never exercised the envelope→fanout→remote path.

Fix (additive, reversible): `EventSink.emit` (`lib/agent_stream.py`) now returns the identity-enriched record it wrote, and the fan-out (`lib/telemetry_delivery.py`) ships that same correlated view to every remote sink. Pinned by a new regression test, `test_envelope_identity_reaches_remote_sinks_not_only_local`.

Gate checks all green: `bash -n` on the four scripts, `py_compile lib/*.py`, and `pytest -q lib` (349 passed). T082's checkbox is flipped to `[x]`; the next unchecked task is T083 (requirements trace).
